{"book":19,"chapter":2,"rubric":"A HEADLESS SERVER / CHAPTER 2","slides":[{"title":"Why packages matter","sub":"Chapter 2 · A headless server","short":"Why","main":"Almost everything on a server came from a package, and an update must not break anything.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Package","Update","KVM host","Two families"],"captions":["A package: an archive of files, metadata and install scripts","An update changes thousands of files, services must not fall over","On a KVM host packages bring the hypervisor, drivers and the agent","Two families: Debian/Ubuntu and the RHEL family"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"files + metadata + scripts","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"files + metadata + scripts","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"thousands of files per update","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"files + metadata + scripts","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"thousands of files per update","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"KVM host: hypervisor from packages","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"files + metadata + scripts","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"thousands of files per update","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"KVM host: hypervisor from packages","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n3","x":180.0,"y":122.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"Debian/Ubuntu and RHEL family","tone":"green","siz